    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Located in the popular Citygate development in Sligo, this two-bedroom apartment offers modern, comfortable living in a highly convenient town-centre location. Situated on the second floor with access via both lift and stairs, the apartment features a spacious and bright open-plan kitchen, dining and living area, flooded with natural light from large windows and a private balcony. The fully fitted kitchen is finished with tiled flooring and a tiled splashback, while the living area benefits from stylish laminate flooring, creating a warm and welcoming space. The property comprises two double bedrooms, one of which enjoys access to a second balcony and includes a en suite whilst a shared bathroom completes this apartment. Just minutes’ walk from Sligo town centre, the apartment is ideally positioned close to a wide range of shops, bars, restaurants, and sports and leisure facilities, as well as being within easy walking distance of Sligo bus and train stations, providing excellent local and national transport links. To arrange a viewing contact Oates Breheny Group on 071-9140404."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Kitchen / Living/ Dining Room (6.1m x 6.1m)\r\nFully fitted kitchen. Laminate flooring. Door to balcony.\r\n\r\nBathroom (3.3m x 2.2m)\r\nTiled flooring. WC & WHB. Shower over bath.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (5.7m x 2.4m)\r\nDouble room. Laminate flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (4.5m x 2.5m)\r\nDouble room. Laminate flooring. Door to balcony.\r\n\r\nEnsuite (2.4m x 2.3m)\r\nTiled flooring. WC & WHB. Shower."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious living accommodation\r\nNew kitchen door & skirting. \r\n2 Balconies. \r\nElectric storage heating.\r\nWithin short walking distance of Sligo town centre, and its shops, bars & restaurants, recreational amenities & church’s.\r\nWalking distance of both primary and secondary schools.\r\nClose proximity of Sligo bus and train station, making local and national transport extremely assessable."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: C2"
      }
